# Backend — patterns

## Database (Drizzle)

Use the shared client and schema:

```typescript
import { db, task } from "@oryxel/db";
```

Prefer typed queries. Keep `+server.ts` / `+page.server.ts` thin; put web-only adapters under `apps/web/src/lib/server/` and reusable domain/database logic in packages.

## API routes — structure

```typescript
import { json, error } from "@sveltejs/kit";
import type { RequestHandler } from "./$types";
import { z } from "zod";

const bodySchema = z.object({
  title: z.string().min(1),
});

export const POST: RequestHandler = async ({ request, locals }) => {
  if (!locals.user) throw error(401, "Unauthorized");

  const body = bodySchema.parse(await request.json());
  // use db ...
  return json({ ok: true });
};
```

## Zod — validation

Validate request bodies and search params where inputs are non-trivial. In Zod v4, `z.record` needs key and value schemas, e.g. `z.record(z.string(), z.string())`.

## Auth

Rely on `event.locals.user` / `event.locals.session` populated in `apps/web/src/hooks.server.ts`. Do not skip session checks on protected endpoints.

## Schema and migrations

1. Edit `packages/db/src/schema.ts` (and run `bun run --cwd apps/web auth:schema` when Better Auth tables change).
2. Run `bun run db:generate` then `bun run db:migrate`. Use `bun run db:push` only for local prototyping, never shared or production databases.

Drizzle config: `packages/db/drizzle.config.ts`. Connection: `DATABASE_URL`.
